2026-05-14  Doug Blank <doug.blank@gmail.com>

	* .github/workflows/gramps-ci.yml, gramps/gen/utils/pypi.py,
	gramps/gen/utils/requirements.py,
	gramps/gen/utils/test/pypi_e2e_test.py,
	gramps/gen/utils/test/pypi_test.py, gramps/gui/plug/_windows.py,
	po/POTFILES.in, po/POTFILES.skip: Add pure-Python PyPI wheel
	installer, replacing pip invocation Replace the subprocess-based pip call in the addon installer with a
	minimal stdlib-only wheel downloader (gramps/gen/utils/pypi.py).
	install_package() fetches wheels from the PyPI JSON API, verifies
	SHA-256, extracts them with zipfile, and recursively installs
	unconditional direct dependencies.  SSL uses ssl.create_default_context() (system trust store) instead
	of certifi, eliminating the missing cacert.pem failure seen in Mac
	bundles.  No external binary (pip, python) is required, so the code
	works correctly in cx_Freeze (Windows AIO) and .app (Mac) bundles
	where sys.executable is not a usable Python interpreter.  Only pure-Python wheels (py3-none-any) are supported; compiled
	extensions are rejected with a clear error message.  Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

